---
import Township from '../layouts/Township.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Township title="Fire & EMS" heading="Fire & EMS" lead="Fernhollow Township Fire and EMS: emergencies, burn permits and station information." eyebrow="Fire & EMS" description="Fernhollow Township Fire and EMS: emergencies, burn permits and station information.">
  <div class="wrap body">
    <div class="callout"><p><strong>In an emergency, call 911.</strong> Do not use the website or email to report an emergency.</p></div>
    <div class="two">
      <div>
        <img class="photo" src="/img/station.svg" alt="Station 1, with the department's engine parked in the middle bay" width="800" height="520" />
        <div class="panel" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
          <h2>Station 1</h2>
          <p>40 Station Road, Fernhollow<br />Non-emergency line: (555) 010-0150</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <section class="svc" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem"><span class="ico"><Icon name="fire" /></span><h2>Burn permits</h2><p>Open burning of yard waste needs a permit from the fire department. Call the station before you burn. No permits are issued on high-wind or dry-weather days.</p></section>
        <section class="svc" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem"><span class="ico"><Icon name="zoning" /></span><h2>Smoke alarm help</h2><p>Residents can ask the department to check or install smoke alarms. Call the non-emergency line to schedule a visit.</p></section>
        <section class="svc"><span class="ico"><Icon name="contact" /></span><h2>Join the department</h2><p>The department welcomes volunteers. Training is provided. <a href="/contact">Contact the township office</a> to get started.</p></section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Township>
